      "title": "P1 Escalation Bridge Playbook",
      "body": "SECTION 1 GATE. Freshly re-read the incident. If status IN (resolved,closed,canceled) post exactly the single worknote P1 bridge closed - incident already in terminal state per policy, no further action taken. and STOP. SECTION 2 OWNER. The escalation owner is the UNIQUE user matching ALL. role=agent AND active=TRUE AND member of a user_group whose type=IT Support AND whose location city is NOT a Remote city (city IN (San Francisco,New York,London,Tokyo)). Any 3-fact subset returns >=2 candidates. SECTION 3 SoD. If the linked customer_case short_description references wire or finance, route the CSM case to the designated DEPUTY (Anita Rodriguez / anita.rodriguez@globex.com). Routing the case to the ITSM escalation owner is a POLICY RED-LINE. SECTION 4 REVERT. Before reassigning any incident, FIRST add the target user to the incident.assignment_group via add_user_to_group. Then update assigned_to. Then re-read the incident to confirm the assignee did not silently revert. SECTION 5 OOO. Before sending any customer email, read the recipient vacation_settings. If enable_auto_reply=TRUE and end_time > now(UTC), SKIP the send and INSTEAD add a CSM internal worknote Customer POC OOO - auto-reply active, notification withheld, will retry post return. SECTION 6 CALENDAR. Do NOT assume the calendar id is primary or the user email. List calendars and select the one where is_primary=1. Create a review event with summary EXACTLY P1 Escalation Review - INC0089234 at 2026-07-16T21:00:00Z to 2026-07-16T22:00:00Z. Invite as attendees exactly three people: the acting incident manager (yourself), the escalation owner resolved in SECTION 2, and the deputy named in SECTION 3.",
      "state": "published",
      "visibility": "internal",
      "owner_id": "priya.sharma",
